   "severity": "medium",
   "summary": "Battle aim: the target prompt takes the panel's first three lines, so only the ability's name shows and the five answers (what it does, how it targets, who) start below the fold (checklist G2)",
   "detail": "Aiming Fireball on iphone17pro the panel shows 'Fireball: choose a target', 'Tap a highlighted tile . tap the slot again to cancel' (two lines) and then the 'Fireball' title, cut at the panel bottom; the damage, targeting and who-it-hits lines sit 500-1100 design px further down and need scrolling. Fix: one prompt line ('Fireball: tap a highlighted foe'); drop the 'tap the slot again to cancel' hint after the first battles (it is a lesson, not a fact), and start the card with what it does.",
